%N A283824 Number of unlabeled trees on n nodes whose unique center is also their unique centroid.
%C A283824 Original name: Number of unlabeled (and unrooted) trees on n nodes having a node that is both a center and a centroid. [This would give a(2) = 1.]
%C A283824 a(n) is the number of trees whose center is a single node equal to the unique centroid. Root the tree at the common center/centroid. Every branch has fewer than n/2 nodes, and the maximum branch height occurs at least twice; such branch multisets correspond bijectively to the trees. - _Damian Faye_, Oct 22 2026
%H A283824 Damian Faye, <a href="/A283824/b283824.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..100</a>
%H A283824 Peter Steinbach, <a href="/A000088/a000088_17.pdf">Field Guide to Simple Graphs, Volume 1</a>, Part 17 (For Volumes 1, 2, 3, 4 of this book see A000088, A008406, A000055, A000664, respectively.). Terms a(11)-a(12) are incorrect.
%H A283824 Peter Steinbach, <a href="/A000055/a000055_12.pdf">Field Guide to Simple Graphs, Volume 3</a>, Part 12 (For Volumes 1, 2, 3, 4 of this book see A000088, A008406, A000055, A000664, respectively.). Terms a(11)-a(12) are incorrect.
%o A283824 (Python)
%o A283824 from networkx import center, nonisomorphic_trees, connected_components
%o A283824 def A283824(n): return 1 if n < 2 else sum(max(map(len,
%o A283824     connected_components(T.subgraph(set(T)-{c[0]}))))*2 < n
%o A283824     for T in nonisomorphic_trees(n) if len(c:=center(T))==1)
